<title>USA: Western Star Trucks issues $110 million in debt.</title>
<headline>Western Star Trucks issues $110 million in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Western Star Trucks Holdings Ltd was priced on Wednesday, according to a high-yield syndicate source.</p>
<p>The deal was increased in size by $10 million, the source</p>
<p>said. Western Star, based in Canada, customizes trucks.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co was lead manager on the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER WESTERN STAR TRUCKS HOLDINGS LTD</p>
<p>AMT $110 MLN	 COUPON 8.75 PCT   MATURITY 5/01/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR UNSEC NTS ISS PRICE 99.503  FIRST PAY DATE 11/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Ba2   YIELD 8.875 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BB-PLUS   SPREAD 212.5 BP   CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
</text>
